# Voxnix eval configuration
# Copy to .env.eval and fill in real values. This file is gitignored.
#
# Evals require two LLM roles:
#   1. Agent-under-test — the Voxnix agent running against a real model
#   2. Judge model — deepeval's LLM-as-judge scoring the agent's output
#
# The eval conftest auto-detects your provider from whichever API key is set.
# Just add a key below — no other configuration needed.
#
# Non-LLM settings (VOXNIX_FLAKE_PATH, TELEGRAM_BOT_TOKEN, etc.) are injected
# automatically by the _mock_settings fixture in conftest.py — no need to set them here.

# ── API key (set exactly one) ───────────────────────────────────
# Priority: OPENAI_API_KEY > OPENROUTER_API_KEY > others.
#
# OPENAI_API_KEY is preferred — deepeval's judge model uses the OpenAI
# client natively, so both the agent-under-test and the judge work with
# zero aliasing.
#
# OPENROUTER_API_KEY is the cheapest option — one key covers both roles.
# conftest aliases it to OPENAI_API_KEY and sets OPENAI_BASE_URL so the
# judge also routes through OpenRouter's OpenAI-compatible endpoint.

# Uncomment one:
# OPENAI_API_KEY=sk-...
OPENROUTER_API_KEY=sk-or-v1-your-key-here
# ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=sk-ant-...
# GOOGLE_API_KEY=AIza...
# XAI_API_KEY=xai-...
# GROQ_API_KEY=gsk_...

# ── Optional: explicit provider override ────────────────────────
# If set, these take precedence over auto-detection. Useful when you
# want to test a specific model that isn't the auto-detected default.
# LLM_PROVIDER=openrouter
# LLM_MODEL=anthropic/claude-haiku-4.5

# ── Additional keys (for cross-model comparison) ────────────────
# Set multiple keys above to enable parametrized testing across
# providers. The eval suite auto-discovers all available keys and
# runs cross-model tests when >1 real provider is configured.
